{
  "dom_id": "step-q175379",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "$x$ is negative **or** an integer, **or** $x$ is greater than $4.$\n\nExpress the compound predicate above in symbolic form given the following notations:\n\n- $N(x):$ $x$ is negative\n\n- $I(x):$ $x$ is an integer\n\n- $G(x):$ $x$ is greater than $4$",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"or\" is represented by the symbol \"$∨.$\"\n\nNote that this sentence consists of two parts: \n\n- **Part 1:** $x$ is negative or an integer. This corresponds to\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is negative}}_{⏟}}_{N}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\,\\text{is an integer }}_{⏟}}_{I},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨I.$\n\n- **Part 2:** $x$ is greater than $4.$ This corresponds to $G.$\n\nSo, we can express the sentence as\n\n$$\n{{x\\,\\text{is negative or an integer }}_{⏟}}_{N∨I}\\,{{\\text{or}}_{⏟}}_{∨}\\,{{x\\text{ is greater than }4}_{⏟}}_{G},\n$$\n\nthat is, $N∨I∨G.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
